<title>USA: Buckeye Partners says ups qtrly cash payout.</title>
<headline>Buckeye Partners says ups qtrly cash payout.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buckeye Partners LP said it approvead a restructuring of its employee stock ownership plan and boosted its quarterly cash payout to unitholders to $0.85 per unit from $0.75 per unit.</p>
<p>The increase in the cash payout will be declared in the quarter after the restructured stock ownership plan is implemented, the company said. That is expected in the first quarter of 1997, it added.  The restructuring involves replacing the plan's current investment in preferred stock of BMC Acquisition Co with about 1.6 million newly issued Buckeye Partners units, the company said.</p>
</text>
